 "difficulty": "Chief Inspector",
 "briefing": "Weather Desk prints a one-line forecast. This time the scariest-looking crew member is innocent, and the imposter looks like the quietest one. One of them talks to the internet and says so out loud. Another says it only prints notes. Do not accuse the loudest. Compare what each one claims with what REA found.",
 "plainBriefing": "Weather Desk shows a one-line forecast. This time the scariest-looking crew member is innocent. One of them talks to the internet on purpose and says so honestly. The liar is a quiet one that says it only writes notes on the screen. Do not accuse the loudest.",
 "hints": [
  "Being scary is not the same as lying. A part that connects to the internet and admits it is telling the truth.",
  "Look for the crew member that says it only prints on the screen, then see whether the scanner found it writing into a file or reading private settings.",
  "It is Diary. It writes a hidden file in your personal folder and reads your private settings. Show both clues."
 ],
 "realLife": "A log file that quietly collects your user name and private settings is a classic leak. The question to ask of any app is not \"does it use the internet?\" but \"does what it does match what it says?\"",
